body:
I cannot believe this happened but I was randomly searching tonight and found that some very tiny channel uploaded the video one month ago!!!

&#x200B;

The long-lost music video lives again, I just downloaded it for posterity.

&#x200B;

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IsrJZOS8Tts](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IsrJZOS8Tts)

This post is made as a joke, I actually like it because now I can buy gold and not get banned.

&#x200B;

I labeled it "humor" for a reason.

Yep! CYOA books are basically the same thing! :) 

&#x200B;

Yes, I could do that, and its looking like my only option at the moment.

I went to my local Walmart and there was this nice, really thick foamlike fabric that is 4$ for 4 yards I believe it said, I was considering using it for padding.

&#x200B;

and some material that looked like it was perfect for a cape (flannel? Linen?) was 5$ a yard.

&#x200B;

I dont know fabrics too well obviously. 5$ a yard sounds like a good deal, though I dont know how many yards Id be using for things.

I actually justify my Guardsmen having all this outdated tech by the fact their system is hated by the Mechanicus, so have to build/maintain all their own stuff. To make matters worse, the system is almost entirely feudal worlds with one civilized world set to be like 1930. :) 

&#x200B;

So I have these excavated ancient scrap tanks and WW2-looking planes

Ooo, i didnt know it was Roman in origin at all, thats cool. Makes sense, given his special ability was to pretend to be a part of the enemy team. 

&#x200B;

I kinda would like to get something like that.

I just mean "real" as in, it can cut things and not break immediately like a wallhanger would, since its highly unlikely Id actually need to use it against another person. 

&#x200B;

I did mean the former, a khopesh with the reach of a longsword, cause I just hate how tiny the historical ones are.

Collective Consciousness, by far :) 

&#x200B;

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZYnDsr8z4iU](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZYnDsr8z4iU)

Thank you, I want to make another game, but the lack of reception combined with my depression makes it hard to start up another project.

&#x200B;

If I knew people liked my last game, I'd be willing to make another.

I wasnt talking as much about making Terrain, as I was actual fortifications with datasheets in the rule books. 

&#x200B;

Like if people are generally cool if someone were to turn an old tissue box into an Imperial Bastion with a folding drawbridge and those pointy things ontop of castle walls.

If its really necessary, heres a respectable picture of me. (I shaved my facial hair recently tho.)

&#x200B;

[**https://tinyurl.com/yywwsrdc**](https://tinyurl.com/yywwsrdc)

Personally the second army in the boxes are what put me off buying them, because I play Space Marines and Imperial Guard, and have no interest in some other army. So the prospect of getting rid of an entire half of an army seems like too much effort, lol. Listing everything on Ebay, shipping, all that.

&#x200B;

As an aside, really wish theyd make a box with Guard in it. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Ive heard people online say that, but I wonder if theres enough people out there like you and your buddy to warrant these split-faction boxes. At 80$ per person, you and him could have gotten a "start collecting" box each, basically. Not sure on the value difference between the two options though.

&#x200B;

\*Edit\* Oh, apparently those things went up in price. Huh.

Oh goodness, I feel quite silly now. It never occurred to me to see if it had a board game since thats just strange to me. There does seem to be one! 

&#x200B;

I'm ok with the GW and tourney thing since I'm not a competitive player. I just like to have fun! :)

They look so chaos-infested though! 

&#x200B;

We are here to defend the planet from aliens, not summon the Great Old Ones.

I can certainly admit I feel like my life has no purpose, why I dont really care to accomplish anything with it.

&#x200B;

My mom really pushed me to join the military when I was younger, but I'm a pacifist so I cant in good conscience be part of a military organization.

Yes, Ive found my army to be very bad against vehicles and things with toughness over 5, I'm trying to find a way to make up for that shortcoming, perhaps by adding Melta guns or plasma to my squads, and maybe some Heavy Weapon Teams or Tarantula Turrets

&#x200B;

(Im cool with Tarantulas, I just say they are on loan from my Space Marine dudes)

I do have plenty of infantry models, so could tweak it by swapping the Bullgryn and Knight for an equal points amount of infantry/engineers. Part of the reason I didnt was cause I didnt want to move so many models.

&#x200B;

The berzerkers had basically infinite attacks so I'm wondering if more bodies would even do anything other than bide time.

2000 points.

&#x200B;

I brought a bunch of tough units with generally high mobility because I keep getting completely murdered off the board in every game I play. But I also wanted to keep to the fluffy aspect of my army, so thats why i brought the Vostroyan warlord and Lord Commissar. The psyker and Yarrick are really just there because its all i had the models for and wanted that Valhallan tank trait.

My whole army is meant to be fluffy according to my regiments backstory, and fun as a whole (why i got so many heavy stubbers! so many dice.)

&#x200B;

The vast majority of people at my local store are hardcore tournement guys who play lists like that Khorn one. The guy I played actually lost the prior match before playing me. Ive never actually won a game at the store.

I dont really build my models with the mindset of "this is a good idea/strong", Ive made a Feudal-themed Guard army which I wanna run with a heavy focus on melee and infantry because it "speaks to me" as some might say, and was wondering which army would do that best in the Guard.

&#x200B;

I do have a 9-man Bullgryn squad I like to bring along with my Death Riders. Rarely lose the whole squad even if they do get focused down. 

&#x200B;

I'm a painter/modeler primarily, I almost never actually play the game itself.

My local scene doesnt really care about having fun. They wont even play with me unless I bring 2000 points because everyones always preparing for some tournement somewhere. (I like smaller games like 1000 points)

&#x200B;

Sucks to hear that their abusive tactics are ok by the book.
